==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|urj-fin-pro|*kirot'ak}}, from {{der|fi|fiu-pro|*kira-}}. Related to {{cog|et|kiruma}} and {{cog|vot|tširota}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-pronunciation|*}}

===Verb===
{{fi-verb}}

# {{lb|fi|intransitive}} To [[curse]], [[swear]], [[damn]].
# {{lb|fi|transitive|+ genitive-accusative}} To [[curse]] someone, [[cast]] a [[spell]] over someone/something, [[enchant]] someone (''negatively'').

====Usage notes====
* The frequentative verb {{m|fi|kiroilla}} is used when the cursing lasts longer, is continuous, is temporally more or less indefinite or the cursing is a habit. On the other hand, {{m|fi||kirota}} is used, for example, when a person says one or a few naughty words in a particular situation. The difference can sometimes be translated in English by using the continuous aspect.

